/*!
\page qxmpp-index.html
\title QXmpp

\section1 Introduction

QXmpp is a cross-platform C++ XMPP client and server library built on top of the
Qt framework (Qt 6.4+). It implements a large number of XMPP Extension Protocols
(XEPs) and exposes a modern, reactive API based on C++20 and Qt's property
system.

\section1 Getting Started

The central class is QXmppClient. Create one, register the managers you need,
then connect:

\code
auto *client = new QXmppClient(this);

// Register managers
auto *pubsub  = client->addNewExtension<QXmppPubSubManager>();
auto *disco   = client->addNewExtension<QXmppDiscoveryManager>();
auto *muc     = client->addNewExtension<QXmppMucManagerV2>();

// Connect
QXmppConfiguration config;
config.setJid("user@example.org");
config.setPassword("secret");
client->connectToServer(config);
\endcode

\section1 Async API

All network operations return a QXmppTask<T>, which represents a pending result.
QXmppTask supports \c co_await, making sequential async code straightforward:

\code
QXmppTask<void> MyManager::doSomething()
{
    auto result = co_await muc->joinRoom("room@conference.example.org", "MyNick").withContext(this);
    if (auto *err = std::get_if<QXmppError>(&result)) {
        qWarning() << "Join failed:" << err->description;
        co_return;
    }
    // continue ...
}
\endcode

Alternatively, use \c .then() to attach a callback:

\code
muc->joinRoom("room@conference.example.org", "MyNick").then(this, [](auto result) {
    if (auto *err = std::get_if<QXmppError>(&result)) {
        qWarning() << "Join failed:" << err->description;
    }
});
\endcode

Results are typically \c QXmpp::Result<T>, a \c std::variant<T, QXmppError>.
Always pass a context object (\c this) to \c .then() or \c .withContext() to
ensure the callback is not invoked after the object has been destroyed.

\section1 Reactive Properties

Selected APIs expose observable state via QBindable<T>, backed by Qt's QProperty system.
QXmppMucRoomV2 is the primary example — room info, config, and participant state are all exposed
as bindable properties that update automatically when the server reports changes:

\code
auto room = *muc->findRoom("room@conference.example.org");
room.setWatchAvatar(true);

// m_avatarNotifier is a QPropertyNotifier member: discarding the handle
// returned by addNotifier() unsubscribes the callback immediately.
m_avatarNotifier = room.avatar().addNotifier([room]() {
    // called whenever the room avatar changes
    auto val = room.avatar().value();
});
\endcode

Observer lifetime, \c addNotifier() versus \c subscribe(), and how to bridge bindable state
into classic signals are covered in \l{Reactive Properties}.

\section1 IQ Requests

IQ stanzas are represented by QXmpp::Iq::Stanza, usually via the aliases
QXmpp::Iq::Get, QXmpp::Iq::Set, QXmpp::Iq::Result and QXmpp::Iq::Error. They are
aggregates with a typed payload, so only the needed fields are set via designated initializers.

QXmppClient::sendIq() sends a get or set request and returns only the payload of the response:
for a get request the same payload type as the request, for a set request QXmpp::Success. Errors
from the other entity are returned as QXmppError.

\code
auto result = co_await client->sendIq(QXmpp::Iq::Get<QXmppDiscoInfo> { .to = u"example.org"_s }).withContext(this);
if (auto *info = std::get_if<QXmppDiscoInfo>(&result)) {
    qDebug() << "Features:" << info->features();
}
\endcode

A payload is any type with a static \c XmlTag, a static \c fromDom() and a \c toXml() function:

\code
struct StatusQuery {
    static constexpr std::tuple XmlTag = { u"status", u"urn:example:status" };
    static std::optional<StatusQuery> fromDom(const QDomElement &el);
    void toXml(QXmlStreamWriter *writer) const;

    QString text;
};
\endcode

Incoming requests are answered by adding a handler to the hook QXmpp::Iq::Received for the type
of the request. The handler returns the payload of the result, QXmpp::Success, a
QXmppStanza::Error or a QXmppTask of them to reply asynchronously:

\code
hooks().add<QXmpp::Iq::Received<QXmpp::Iq::Get<StatusQuery>>>([this](QXmpp::Iq::Get<StatusQuery> &&iq) {
    return StatusQuery { .text = m_status };
});
\endcode

End-to-end encryption of IQs is opt-in via QXmpp::Iq::SendOptions and selected via the
QXmpp::Iq::SelectEncryption hook. Replies to encrypted requests are encrypted the same way.

\section1 Hooks

Extensions are connected via hooks instead of virtual functions or signals. A hook is a type
with a name and a handler signature; any extension (or the application) can add handlers to the
hooks of the client. Handlers can run asynchronously, stop further handlers, be keyed (e.g. per
PubSub node) or be the single responder of a hook. See QXmpp::Hooks for the details.

Extensions add their handlers in their constructor via QXmppClientExtension::hooks(), the
application via QXmppClient::hooks(). Handlers are removed when their owner is destroyed:

\code
// announce a feature via service discovery
client->hooks(this).add<QXmpp::Disco::CollectInfo>([](QList<QString> &features, QList<QXmppDiscoIdentity> &) {
    features.append(u"urn:example:status"_s);
});
\endcode

Important hooks of QXmpp:
\list
\li QXmpp::Iq::Received: incoming IQ requests
\li QXmpp::Messages::Received: incoming messages after decryption
\li QXmpp::Messages::SelectEncryption, QXmpp::Iq::SelectEncryption: end-to-end encryption of
    outgoing messages and IQs
\li QXmpp::Disco::CollectInfo: features and identities of the client
\li QXmpp::PubSub::EventReceived: PubSub event notifications, per node
\li QXmpp::Mam::MessageReceived: messages of archive queries
\li QXmpp::Connection::StanzaReceived: all other incoming stanzas
\li QXmpp::Connection::SessionStarted, QXmpp::Connection::SessionEnded: start and end of a
    session, also across stream resumption
\endlist

\section1 Messages and End-to-End Encryption

Incoming messages from the stream, message carbons and archive queries run through the message
pipeline (see QXmpp::Messages): the real sender is resolved (e.g. in MUC rooms), the message is
decrypted and the QXmpp::Messages::Received hook is run with its QXmpp::Messages::Context.
Messages not consumed by a handler are delivered via QXmppClient::messageReceived(), also those
of rooms joined via QXmppMucManagerV2. Messages of archive queries are returned by
QXmppMamManager::retrieve().

Messages sent via QXmppClient::sendMessage() or QXmppClient::send() run through the outgoing
pipeline. The application selects the end-to-end encryption via the
QXmpp::Messages::SelectEncryption hook:

\code
client->hooks(this).add<QXmpp::Messages::SelectEncryption>([this](QXmpp::Messages::EncryptionSelection &selection) {
    if (isEncryptionEnabled(selection.to())) {
        selection.setEncryption(QXmpp::E2ee::Omemo2);
    }
});
\endcode

QXmppClient::sendMessage() reports in QXmpp::Messages::Sent how the message has been processed:
the encryption actually used, the recipients, whether the delivery has been confirmed and, for
MUC rooms and MIX channels, the ID of the message in their archive. Messages to rooms and
channels finish after their reflection.

\code
QXmppMessage message;
message.setTo(u"room@conference.example.org"_s);
message.setType(QXmppMessage::GroupChat);
message.setBody(u"Hello!"_s);

auto result = co_await client->sendMessage(std::move(message)).withContext(this);
if (auto *sent = std::get_if<QXmpp::Messages::Sent>(&result)) {
    // sent->deliveryState(), sent->archiveId(), ...
}
\endcode

Encryptions are implemented as providers registered via QXmpp::E2ee::Providers, which decrypt
incoming and encrypt outgoing messages and IQs. QXmppOmemoManager is the provider for OMEMO.

\section1 Managers

Managers are the primary way to use XMPP features. Register them with
QXmppClient and extend QXmppClient by subclassing QXmppClientExtension. See the
\l{qxmpp-managers}{Managers} module for the full list.

\section2 Messaging
\list
\li QXmppCarbonManagerV2 — Message carbons (\xepn{0280})
\li QXmppMamManager — Message archive management (\xepn{0313})
\li QXmppMessageReceiptManager — Message delivery receipts (\xepn{0184})
\li QXmppAttentionManager — Attention requests (\xepn{0224})
\endlist

\section2 Contacts and Roster
\list
\li QXmppRosterManager — Contact list (\xepn{0162})
\li QXmppVCardManager — vCards (vcard-temp)
\li QXmppUserLocationManager — User location (\xepn{0080})
\li QXmppUserTuneManager — User tune (\xepn{0118})
\li QXmppVersionManager — Software version (\xepn{0092})
\li QXmppEntityTimeManager — Entity time (\xepn{0202})
\endlist

\section2 Groupchat
\list
\li QXmppMucManagerV2 — Multi-user chat with reactive API (\xepn{0045})
\li QXmppMixManager — Mediated Information eXchange (\xepn{0369})
\endlist

\section2 File Sharing
\list
\li QXmppFileSharingManager — Stateless file sharing (\xepn{0447})
\li QXmppHttpUploadManager — HTTP file upload service (\xepn{0363})
\li QXmppUploadRequestManager — HTTP upload slot requests (\xepn{0363})
\li QXmppTransferManager — In-band / SOCKS5 file transfer (\xepn{0047}, \xepn{0065})
\endlist

\section2 End-to-End Encryption
\list
\li QXmppOmemoManager — OMEMO 2 end-to-end encryption (\xepn{0384})
\li QXmppAtmManager — Automatic trust management (\xepn{0450})
\li QXmppTrustManager — Trust level storage and queries
\endlist

\section2 Calls
\list
\li QXmppCallManager — Jingle audio/video calls (\xepn{0166})
\li QXmppCallInviteManager — Call invites (\xepn{0482})
\li QXmppJingleMessageInitiationManager — Jingle message initiation (\xepn{0353})
\endlist

\section2 Bookmarks and PubSub
\list
\li QXmppPepBookmarkManager — PEP native bookmarks (\xepn{0402})
\li QXmppPubSubManager — Publish-subscribe (\xepn{0060})
\endlist

\section2 Service Discovery and Utilities
\list
\li QXmppDiscoveryManager — Service discovery (\xepn{0030})
\li QXmppBlockingManager — Contact blocking (\xepn{0191})
\li QXmppExternalServiceDiscoveryManager — External service discovery (\xepn{0215})
\li QXmppRegistrationManager — In-band registration (\xepn{0077})
\li QXmppAccountMigrationManager — Account data migration (\xepn{0227})
\li QXmppMovedManager — Account migration hints (\xepn{0283})
\li QXmppNetworkMonitor — Reconnection on network changes (QNetworkInformation)
\endlist

\section2 Legacy (deprecated)
\list
\li QXmppMucManager — superseded by QXmppMucManagerV2
\li QXmppCarbonManager — superseded by QXmppCarbonManagerV2
\li QXmppBookmarkManager — superseded by QXmppPepBookmarkManager
\li QXmppArchiveManager — superseded by QXmppMamManager
\li \l QXmppRpcManager — RPC (\xepn{0009})
\endlist

\section1 Low-Level Stanza API

For direct access to XMPP stanzas:
\list
\li QXmpp::Iq::Stanza (QXmpp::Iq::Get, QXmpp::Iq::Set, QXmpp::Iq::Result,
    QXmpp::Iq::Error): typed IQ stanzas
\li QXmppMessage
\li QXmppPresence
\endlist

